texts.NKJV:
My voice You shall hear in the morning, O Lord;
In the morning I will direct it to You,
And I will look up.

texts.ESV:
Lead me, O Lord, in your righteousness
    because of my enemies;
    make your way straight before me.

texts.NASB95:
There is nothing reliable in what they say;
Their inward part is destruction itself.
Their throat is an open grave;
They flatter with their tongue.

texts.NKJV:
For there is no faithfulness in their mouth;
Their inward part is destruction;
Their throat is an open tomb;
They flatter with their tongue.

texts.ESV:
For there is no truth in their mouth;
    their inmost self is destruction;
their throat is an open grave;
    they flatter with their tongue.

Make them bear their guilt, O God;
    let them fall by their own counsels;
because of the abundance of their transgressions cast them out,
    for they have rebelled against you.

texts.NKJV:
But let all those rejoice who put their trust in You;
Let them ever shout for joy, because You defend them;
Let those also who love Your name
Be joyful in You.

texts.ESV:
But let all who take refuge in you rejoice;
    let them ever sing for joy,
and spread your protection over them,
    that those who love your name may exult in you.

texts.NASB95:
I am weary with my sighing;
Every night I make my bed swim,
I dissolve my couch with my tears.

texts.NKJV:
I am weary with my groaning;
All night I make my bed swim;
I drench my couch with my tears.

texts.ESV:
I am weary with my moaning;
    every night I flood my bed with tears;
    I drench my couch with my weeping.

texts.NKJV:
O Lord my God, in You I put my trust;
Save me from all those who persecute me;
And deliver me,

texts.NASB95:
Let the enemy pursue my soul and overtake it;
And let him trample my life down to the ground
And lay my glory in the dust. Selah.

texts.NKJV:
Let the enemy pursue me and overtake me;
Yes, let him trample my life to the earth,
And lay my honor in the dust. Selah

texts.ESV:
let the enemy pursue my soul and overtake it,
    and let him trample my life to the ground
    and lay my glory in the dust. Selah

texts.NASB95:
Arise, O Lord, in Your anger;
Lift up Yourself against the rage of my adversaries,
And arouse Yourself for me; You have appointed judgment.

texts.NKJV:
Arise, O Lord, in Your anger;
Lift Yourself up because of the rage of my enemies;
Rise up for me to the judgment You have commanded!

texts.ESV:
Arise, O Lord, in your anger;
    lift yourself up against the fury of my enemies;
    awake for me; you have appointed a judgment.

texts.NKJV:
The Lord shall judge the peoples;
Judge me, O Lord, according to my righteousness,
And according to my integrity within me.

texts.ESV:
The Lord judges the peoples;
    judge me, O Lord, according to my righteousness
    and according to the integrity that is in me.

texts.NKJV:
Oh, let the wickedness of the wicked come to an end,
But establish the just;
For the righteous God tests the hearts and minds.

If he does not turn back,
He will sharpen His sword;
He bends His bow and makes it ready.

You have rebuked the nations,
You have destroyed the wicked;
You have blotted out their name forever and ever.

texts.NASB95:
The enemy has come to an end in perpetual ruins,
And You have uprooted the cities;
The very memory of them has perished.

texts.NKJV:
O enemy, destructions are finished forever!
And you have destroyed cities;
Even their memory has perished.

texts.ESV:
The enemy came to an end in everlasting ruins;
    their cities you rooted out;
    the very memory of them has perished.

texts.NASB95:
Be gracious to me, O Lord;
See my affliction from those who hate me,
You who lift me up from the gates of death,

The Lord has made Himself known;
He has executed judgment.
In the work of his own hands the wicked is snared. Higgaion Selah.

texts.NKJV:
The Lord is known by the judgment He executes;
The wicked is snared in the work of his own hands.
Meditation. Selah

Arise, O Lord,
Do not let man prevail;
Let the nations be judged in Your sight.

Hear a just cause, O Lord,
Attend to my cry;
Give ear to my prayer which is not from deceitful lips.

texts.NASB95:
You have tried my heart;
You have visited me by night;
You have tested me and You find nothing;
I have purposed that my mouth will not transgress.

texts.NKJV:
You have tested my heart;
You have visited me in the night;
You have tried me and have found nothing;
I have purposed that my mouth shall not transgress.

texts.ESV:
You have tried my heart, you have visited me by night,
    you have tested me, and you will find nothing;
    I have purposed that my mouth will not transgress.

texts.NKJV:
Arise, O Lord,
Confront him, cast him down;
Deliver my life from the wicked with Your sword,

texts.ESV:
from men by your hand, O Lord,
    from men of the world whose portion is in this life.
You fill their womb with treasure;
    they are satisfied with children,
    and they leave their abundance to their infants.

Vindicate me, O Lord,
    for I have walked in my integrity,
    and I have trusted in the Lord without wavering.

texts.NASB95:
Requite them according to their work and according to the evil of their practices;
Requite them according to the deeds of their hands;
Repay them their recompense.

texts.NKJV:
Give them according to their deeds,
And according to the wickedness of their endeavors;
Give them according to the work of their hands;
Render to them what they deserve.

texts.ESV:
Give to them according to their work
    and according to the evil of their deeds;
give to them according to the work of their hands;
    render them their due reward.

texts.NASB95:
The Lord is my strength and my shield;
My heart trusts in Him, and I am helped;
Therefore my heart exults,
And with my song I shall thank Him.

texts.NKJV:
The Lord is my strength and my shield;
My heart trusted in Him, and I am helped;
Therefore my heart greatly rejoices,
And with my song I will praise Him.

texts.ESV:
The Lord is my strength and my shield;
    in him my heart trusts, and I am helped;
my heart exults,
    and with my song I give thanks to him.

By your favor, O Lord,
    you made my mountain stand strong;
you hid your face;
    I was dismayed.

You have turned for me my mourning into dancing;
    you have loosed my sackcloth
    and clothed me with gladness,

texts.NASB95:
Let destruction come upon him unawares,
And let the net which he hid catch himself;
Into that very destruction let him fall.

texts.NKJV:
Let destruction come upon him unexpectedly,
And let his net that he has hidden catch himself;
Into that very destruction let him fall.

texts.ESV:
Let destruction come upon him when he does not know it!
And let the net that he hid ensnare him;
    let him fall into it—to his destruction!

texts.NASB95:
But as for me, when they were sick, my clothing was sackcloth;
I humbled my soul with fasting,
And my prayer kept returning to my bosom.

texts.NKJV:
But as for me, when they were sick,
My clothing was sackcloth;
I humbled myself with fasting;
And my prayer would return to my own heart.

texts.ESV:
But I, when they were sick—
    I wore sackcloth;
    I afflicted myself with fasting;
I prayed with head bowed on my chest.

I went about as though I grieved for my friend or my brother;
as one who laments his mother,
    I bowed down in mourning.

texts.NASB95:
But at my stumbling they rejoiced and gathered themselves together;
The smiters whom I did not know gathered together against me,
They slandered me without ceasing.

texts.NKJV:
But in my adversity they rejoiced
And gathered together;
Attackers gathered against me,
And I did not know it;
They tore at me and did not cease;

texts.ESV:
But at my stumbling they rejoiced and gathered;
    they gathered together against me;
wretches whom I did not know
    tore at me without ceasing;

They open wide their mouths against me;
    they say, “Aha, Aha!
    Our eyes have seen it!”

texts.NKJV:
This You have seen, O Lord;
Do not keep silence.
O Lord, do not be far from me.

texts.NASB95:
Let them shout for joy and rejoice, who favor my vindication;
And let them say continually, “The Lord be magnified,
Who delights in the prosperity of His servant.”

Those who seek my life lay snares for me;
And those who seek to injure me have threatened destruction,
And they devise treachery all day long.

texts.NKJV:
Those also who seek my life lay snares for me;
Those who seek my hurt speak of destruction,
And plan deception all the day long.

texts.ESV:
Those who seek my life lay their snares;
    those who seek my hurt speak of ruin
    and meditate treachery all day long.

texts.NKJV:
I was mute with silence,
I held my peace even from good;
And my sorrow was stirred up.

texts.ESV:
I was mute and silent;
    I held my peace to no avail,
and my distress grew worse.

texts.NASB95:
My heart was hot within me,
While I was musing the fire burned;
Then I spoke with my tongue:

texts.NKJV:
My heart was hot within me;
While I was musing, the fire burned.
Then I spoke with my tongue:

texts.ESV:
My heart became hot within me.
As I mused, the fire burned;
    then I spoke with my tongue:

texts.NASB95:
“Lord, make me to know my end
And what is the extent of my days;
Let me know how transient I am.

texts.ESV:
“O Lord, make me know my end
    and what is the measure of my days;
    let me know how fleeting I am!

texts.NASB95:
“Behold, You have made my days as handbreadths,
And my lifetime as nothing in Your sight;
Surely every man at his best is a mere breath. Selah.

texts.NKJV:
Indeed, You have made my days as handbreadths,
And my age is as nothing before You;
Certainly every man at his best state is but vapor. Selah

texts.NASB95:
“Surely every man walks about as a phantom;
Surely they make an uproar for nothing;
He amasses riches and does not know who will gather them.

texts.NKJV:
Surely every man walks about like a shadow;
Surely they busy themselves in vain;
He heaps up riches,
And does not know who will gather them.

texts.ESV:
Surely a man goes about as a shadow!
Surely for nothing they are in turmoil;
    man heaps up wealth and does not know who will gather!

texts.NASB95:
“With reproofs You chasten a man for iniquity;
You consume as a moth what is precious to him;
Surely every man is a mere breath. Selah.

texts.NKJV:
When with rebukes You correct man for iniquity,
You make his beauty melt away like a moth;
Surely every man is vapor. Selah

texts.NASB95:
“Hear my prayer, O Lord, and give ear to my cry;
Do not be silent at my tears;
For I am a stranger with You,
A sojourner like all my fathers.

texts.NKJV:
“Hear my prayer, O Lord,
And give ear to my cry;
Do not be silent at my tears;
For I am a stranger with You,
A sojourner, as all my fathers were.
